// the SINGLE source of truth for which guardians are SEA creatures. Sea lairs draw only from these;
// LAND lairs must exclude all of them. Giant Barnacle) leaked onto land groves.
// ── THEMATIC LAIR NAMES ────
// Names are now drawn from pools that belong to the GUARDIAN: every beast gets a den, every undead
// a barrow, every dragon a hoard, and the named great powers get signature lairs of their own. Each
// guardian has at least three names it could be found in; pools are shared by category, so two
// different beasts may both be found in a "Blood-Slick Warren" — which is the intent.
//
// Names are also made UNIQUE within a world. The Chronicle tints lair names by difficulty through a
// global name -> colour registry with first-registered-wins, so when 68 of 81 names were reused at
// different grades (measured on a 14x10 map) most lairs showed the wrong difficulty colour while
// their guardian showed the right one. That is the "lair and guardian are different colours"
// report. Unique names fix it at the root, and incidentally let a player tell three lairs apart in
// one report.
